==Trivia==
* Sound is the first fan-made fruit to be added to the game. The original concept was created by @Aqu4G (on X/Twitter), one of the winners of the first fan fruit/art contest. The second is the [[Kitsune]] fruit.
* Many of Sound's moves contain musical vocabulary, such as Tempo (rate of speed of music played), Prestissimo (very fast) or Fortissimo (very loud).
* While using {{Ability|F}}, the user can fly faster (or even faster with the Tempo Meter activated) when on low [[health]], but not as fast as [[Venom]] (it also has the same flight mechanic). [[Blade]] also shares this mechanic, although it is less noticeable.
* Sound is the second least expensive fruit to have a [[Power Meter|meter]], but also a variable [[Power Meter|meter]].
** Sound is also one of the fruits that have [[Power Meter|meters]] that are not intended for transformation, with the others being [[Gravity]], [[Shadow]], [[Creation]], [[Eagle]], [[Pain]], [[Spirit]] and [[Control]].
* Sound fruit is currently bugged. After charging the tempo meter, the gold shield does not appear. After [[Updates/30]], when Symphony Radiance launches the disco ball and lands, it won't make the full sound.

